      "Activity Description": "Threat modeling is thinking through how a system could be attacked so you can defend it. It is imagining trouble on purpose.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Finding weaknesses before attackers do protects users and their data.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It feeds the network architecture and supports information security work.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Map the system, list how it could be attacked, and rank the risks. Capture the model in Notion.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "OWASP, the open community for software security: https://owasp.org/"
    },
