      "Activity Description": "Penetration testing is safely trying to break into a system to find its weak spots. It is a controlled attack to expose gaps.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Real-world testing reveals holes that reviews on paper miss.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It feeds the network architecture and supports security work.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "With permission, probe the system for vulnerabilities and document each one. Record findings in Notion.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "OWASP, the open community for software security: https://owasp.org/"
    },
