      "Activity Description": "Firewall configuration is setting the rules for what traffic a system allows or blocks. It is the gatekeeper for a network.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "A well-configured firewall keeps out unwanted access while letting the right traffic through.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It feeds the network architecture and supports security work.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Define which traffic is allowed and block the rest, then test the rules. Document the setup in Notion.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "OWASP, the open community for software security: https://owasp.org/"
    },
