      ],
      "Activity Description": "Sprint retrospective facilitation is guiding the team's reflection at a sprint's end on what went well and what to improve. It is how a team learns from itself.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Retrospectives are where continuous improvement actually happens, so the team gets better each cycle.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens across sprints and produces retro action items and maturity measurements. It is a team workshop.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Create a safe space, gather honest reflections, and agree on a few changes. Run it in FigJam or Trello.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
