      ],
      "Activity Description": "Identifying research patterns is spotting the themes that repeat across research. It is finding the signal in the noise.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Patterns tell the team what is common and important, so they act on real trends.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens in discovery and acceptance testing and feeds research analysis.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Review your findings and group what repeats into clear themes. Cluster them in FigJam.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/"
    },
