      "Activity Description": "User story generation is writing needs as short statements from the user's point of view. It keeps the focus on the person, not the feature.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Stories break big requirements into small, buildable pieces the team can pick up one at a time.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens in requirements and produces user story statements.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Write each need as who wants what and why, with clear acceptance criteria. Capture them in Notion or Trello.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
