      "Activity Description": "Analyzing project risk is spotting what could go wrong and planning how to handle it. It is looking for trouble on purpose, early.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Spotting risks ahead of time lets a team prevent or soften problems instead of scrambling.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens across the project and feeds the project plan and risk analysis.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "List what could go wrong, rate each risk, and plan a response. Track it in Notion.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
