      "Activity Description": "Creating acceptance criteria is writing the plain conditions that define when work is done. It sets a shared finish line.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Agreed criteria end the debate about whether something is finished.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens in requirements and produces acceptance criteria, task flows, and scope.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "For each item, list what must be true to accept it. Write them in Notion or Trello with the team.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
