      "Activity Description": "Defining UX design operations is setting up how a team's design work runs, from files to systems to process. It keeps design work organized and consistent.",
      "Why Is This Activity Important?": "Solid design ops let designers focus on design instead of wrestling with process.",
      "How Does the Activity Relate to Milestones and Deliverables and Workshops?": "It happens at intake and produces the team process map.",
      "How To Complete the Activity": "Standardize the files, systems, and steps the design team uses. Document it in Notion or FigJam.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    }
